    "content": "## Core Concept Have you ever struggled to find the right element on a webpage? Locators like getByText and getByLabel can simplify this process. These tools help you interact with elements based on their text or associated labels. How do you currently handle element selection in your tests? ## Key Rules - Use getByText for elements with specific visible text. - Use getByLabel for form controls associated with labels, enhancing accessibility. - Always ensure your text or label is unique to avoid ambiguity. ## ???? Try This ```js const button = await page.getByText('Submit'); await button.click(); const input = await page.getByLabel('Email'); await input.fill('test@example.com'); ``` ## ??? Quick Quiz Q: What locator would you use for a button labeled 'Log In'? A: getByText('Log In') ## ???? Key Takeaway Choosing the right locator is key to writing reliable and maintainable tests!"
