    "createdAt": "2026-04-03T09:45:44.930Z",
    "level": "beginner",
    "content": "## Core Concept Have you ever felt restricted by the types in your functions? Generics in TypeScript allow you to create flexible and reusable components. What???s your experience with them? ## Key Rules - Use `T` to represent a type parameter for flexibility. - Define interfaces for better structure and type safety. - Combine generics with interfaces to enhance code reusability and clarity. ## ???? Try This ```js function identity<T>(arg: T): T { return arg; } interface Container<T> { value: T; } ``` ## ??? Quick Quiz Q: What is the main benefit of using generics? A: They allow for type-safe, reusable code without sacrificing flexibility. ## ???? Key Takeaway Embrace generics to write cleaner, more maintainable TypeScript code!"
