    "createdAt": "2026-04-03T09:43:45.042Z",
    "level": "beginner",
    "content": "## Core Concept Have you ever wished your functions could handle multiple data types without losing type safety? That's where generics come into play! They allow you to create reusable components that work with any data type, making your code cleaner and more adaptable. ## Key Rules - Use angle brackets <> to define generic type parameters. - Apply constraints using the 'extends' keyword to limit types. - Remember, generics can be used in functions, classes, and interfaces. ## ???? Try This ```js function identity<T>(arg: T): T { return arg; } const num = identity<number>(5); const str = identity<string>('Hello'); ``` ## ??? Quick Quiz Q: What keyword is used to apply constraints to generic types? A: 'extends' ## ???? Key Takeaway Generics are a powerful tool in TypeScript that enhance type safety while keeping your code flexible."
