    "level": "beginner",
    "content": "## Core Concept Have you ever faced the hassle of checking if a function argument is provided? Default function parameters can save you from that extra boilerplate! What do you think about using them in your code? ## Key Rules - Default parameters are defined in the function signature. - They can be any valid expression, including other parameters. - They allow your functions to be more flexible and concise. ## ???? Try This ```js function greet(name = 'Guest') { return `Hello, ${name}!`; } console.log(greet()); // Hello, Guest! ``` ## ??? Quick Quiz Q: What happens if you pass `undefined` as an argument? A: The default parameter will be used. ## ???? Key Takeaway Embrace default parameters to write cleaner and more resilient functions!"
